{
 "schema": 1,
 "name": "Painbringer enrages the Reaper when a Reaped Soul is generated",
 "contract": "Painbringer 680995 promises that generating a Reaped Soul has a 10% chance to trigger Masochistic Rage 570097 for 5 seconds, and to extend it by 3 seconds when it is already up. It is two SPELL_AURA_PROC_TRIGGER_SPELL effects - 520533 applies, 520877 extends - and its record carries ProcTypeMask 0, so LoadSpellProcs makes no entry and the aura never sees an event. A spell_proc row could not carry it either, because generating a Reaped Soul is not a proc event the core knows: the module answers it where it already recognises a newly harvested soul for Soul Splinters. The chance is the talent's own ProcChance and both durations are its children's own values. Reaped Soul holds three stacks and a grant at the cap is not a generation, so the awards alternate - one spent, one generated - and eighty generations go through the same function the game calls. A run where the talent never fires is 0.9^80, under a hundredth of one per cent.",
 "timeout_ms": 180000,
 "players": [
  { "id": "reaper", "race": 10, "class": 30, "level": 80 }
 ],
